+A verdict is recorded on the current delivery by an agent holding the `qa`
+role for the lot's project. It is refused when the same identity is the lot
+assignee, the delivery author or the proof author (`qa-same-actor`), and the
+SQL guard enforces this for both drivers and direct storage calls:
+
+```sh
+ameesh module it qa 123 --sha256 <digest> --verdict ok \
+                       --scope install,login --report https://ci.example/run/42
+```
+
+`--verdict ok` opens the gate for the delivery it is bound to; `blocked`
+keeps it closed. A new delivery declaration invalidates the verdict, even
+when the bytes are identical. The audit reports `missing_qa` (no current
+`ok` verdict) and `stale_qa` (verdict bound to an earlier delivery) as
